            {
              "id": "ec2d2b74-1050-4132-8081-152237982933",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>The Cultural Legacy of the Royal Game of the Goose: 400 years of Printed Board Games </strong></em>was written by Adrian Seville, published by Amsterdam University Press, July 1, 2019."
            },
            {
              "id": "d92bf964-cbb7-47e2-8828-816e2dceea3e",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "86c792d7-1834-4728-bc18-66f039df8ccb",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "<em>The</em> Game of the Goose<em> is one of the oldest printed </em><a href=\"#/board-game\"><em>board games</em></a><em>, dating back 400 years. It has spawned thousands of derivatives: simple race games, played with </em><a href=\"#/dice\"><em>dice</em></a><em>, on themes that mirror much of human activity. Its legacy can be traced in </em><a href=\"#/educational-games\"><em>games of education</em></a><em>, advertising and polemic, as well as in those of amusement and </em><a href=\"#/gambling\"><em>gambling</em></a><em> - and games on new themes are still being developed. This book, by the leading international </em><a href=\"#/collectibles\"><em>collector</em></a><em> of the </em><a href=\"#/genre\"><em>genre</em></a><em>, is devoted to showing why the </em>Game of the Goose<em> is special and why it can lay claim to being the most influential of any printed game in the cultural history of Europe. Detailed study of the games reveals their historical provenance and - reversing the process - gives unusual insights into the cultures which produced them. They therefore provide rich sources for the cultural historian. This book is beautifully illustrated with more than 90 illustrations, many in color, which are integrated throughout the text.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "fb952c01-5bf7-4e00-b62e-13b5b53337b7",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
          ]
